  {
    "index": 3,
    "hash": "9/IX4BYgBiM8HPgX3W833DO8ACE=",
    "timestampUtcMs": "2026-08-19T11:30:39.266Z",
    "action": {
      "type": "SET_CONTENT",
      "input": {
        "content": "Netcompany's business model is bespoke build and it owns the client relationship, and the research reads that combination as making it the closest competitor rather than a channel. It was previously ranked first in Denmark.\n\nThe distinction turns on who holds the client. Most leads in this set deliver into relationships a platform can sit inside; Netcompany's model is to own both the build and the relationship, so anything it adopted would be adopted as its own capability rather than resold onward. At 7,800+ people it is also well past the size at which a first partner is workable.\n\nThe corroborating detail sits elsewhere in this corpus: Netcompany is the buyer that acquired SDC, the member-bank-owned Danish cooperative. It is consolidating the same Nordic market this lead set is trying to enter.\n\n---\n\n## Leads sharing this finding (1)\n\n**unprioritised**\n- Netcompany (DK \u00b7 7,800+)\n\nVerbatim research text this claim was extracted from:\n\n> WAS DK #1. Bespoke build is its business model and it owns the client relationship. Closest competitor, not a channel.",
        "updatedAt": "2026-08-19T11:30:39.266670Z"
      },
      "timestampUtcMs": "2026-08-19T11:30:39.266674Z"
    }
  },
